    "text": "A bag contains <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> white and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math> black balls. Three balls are drawn at random from the bag. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math> be the number of white balls, among the drawn balls. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>&#963;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is the variance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><msup><mi>&#963;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is equal to",
    "image": null
